[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have this code:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">BigOperators</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">BigOperators</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SetNotation</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- noncomputable def G_certificate := Fintype.ofFinite G -- still fails to synthesize</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- every inverse is unique, so {g | g ∈ G} = {g⁻¹ | g ∈ G}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hxinv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_bijective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·⁻¹</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">And</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_surjective</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_univ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">implies_true</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hi</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inv_inv</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- do some rewriting to match the assumptions of Finset.prod_mul_prod_comm</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rhs</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hxinv</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_mul_prod_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·⁻¹</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">))]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">one_mul</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">id_eq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_inv_cancel</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- the product of a finite number of 1s is 1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_eq_one</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_one</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I want to know more about how to correctly assume that G is finite. I believe that ideally I'd be able to work with the declaration <code>variable (G : Type*) [CommGroup G] [Finite G]</code>.</p>\n<p>In fact, that <code>[Finite G]</code> declaration isn't used at all, and the example still compiles without problem if I comment it out. It appears to be substituted by the \"implicit\" declaration <code>{_ : Fintype G}</code> on the statement of the example itself. That can't be removed; whether <code>[Finite G]</code> is declared or not, the ∏ notation will complain about being unable to synthesize a Fintype instance if I don't have <code>{_ : Fintype G}</code>.</p>\n<p>My read of the documentation ( <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finite#doc\">docs#Finite</a> ) is that I'm supposed to get a Fintype instance from a Finite instance by using <code>Fintype.ofFinite</code>. Is that correct? If so, how do I do that in a way that is accessible to the set product notation in the statement of the example?</p>",
        "id": 576550679,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael",
        "timestamp": 1772396513
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>From the docstring for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finite#doc\">docs#Finite</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Theorems should use <code>Finite</code> instead of <code>Fintype</code>, unless definitions in the theorem statement require <code>Fintype</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The statement requires <code>Fintype</code>, so you should assume <code>[Fintype G]</code>.</p>",
        "id": 576551124,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1772396859
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, fair enough! Thanks for pointing it out.</p>",
        "id": 576551202,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael",
        "timestamp": 1772396947
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- why import random things, just import everything</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `x` is a distraction; remove it</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">subst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- use results in the library rather than reproving them manually</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_eq_iff_mul_eq_one</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_inv_distrib</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prod_bijective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·⁻¹</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">inv_injective</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv_surjective</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 576558887,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
